 transactions execute concurrently.","status":"documented_fact","support":[{"url":"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html","title":"Write-Ahead Logging","passage":"However, since there is only one WAL file, there can only be one writer at a time.","locator":"2.2 Concurrency","sourceType":"Primary documentation","responseId":"mtqvh286k8nqsk"}],"method":"Documented WAL locking model only; no workload, transaction duration, filesystem, or checkpoint configuration was measured.","comparability":"Directly relevant to the defined overlapping-write requirement, but it does not quantify contention or latency.","confidence":"High for the single-writer limitation because the official WAL page was retrieved; no performance conclusion is made.","disposition":"retain"},"eligibleForReview":true,"receiptPath":"/home/balauru/.pi-profiles/fabric/tmp/fabric-research-rework-review/behavior-evaluator-final/live-run-20260328-a-cde/worker-backups.json","checked":false},{"key":"backups/postgres-online-base-backup","assignment":"backups","row":{"id":"postgres-online-base-backup","slot":"backup","finding":"PostgreSQL documents pg_basebackup as taking a base backup from a running cluster without affecting other database clients, usable as a basis for point-in-time recovery or a standby.","status":"documented_fact","support":[{"url":"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html","title":"pg_basebackup","passage":"pg_basebackup is used to take a base backup of a running PostgreSQL database cluster. These are taken without affecting other clients to the database, and can be used both for point-in-time recovery and as the starting point for a log-shipping or streaming-replication standby server.","locator":"Description","sourceType":"Primary documentation","responseId":"mtqvh286k8nqsk"}],"method":"Documented physical-cluster backup behavior. It does not establish that a particular backup command, WAL-retention setting, or restore procedure is correct for a deployment.","comparability":